Ladybird checks an IOSurface’s row alignment only before it makes a
Metal texture over a decoded image frame, whose surface may come from
another process. Over its own surfaces, and over video frames, it makes
a texture whatever the alignment of their rows.

WebKit makes its IOSurface textures with no such check, both in its
GraphicsContextGLCocoa::createExternalImage() and in the WebGPU method
Device::newTextureWithDescriptor(). So does the Dawn that Blink uses, in
Texture::InitializeFromIOSurface(). And Gecko binds its IOSurfaces to
OpenGL textures in MacIOSurface::BindTexImage(), also unchecked.
